  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "What’s the Deal with ADA-Style Shower Seat Heights?",
    "text": "What’s the Deal with ADA-Style Shower Seat Heights?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "You've probably heard talk about ADA-style shower seat heights, and it's a good question to explore, especially if you're looking to enhance your bathroom's accessibility. So, what's the deal? Basically, many manufacturer guides and accessibility standards suggest an ADA-style seat height that falls between 17 and 19 inches above the finished floor. This range isn't just arbitrary; it's designed to make transferring to and from the seat easier and safer for individuals with mobility challenges. However, it's super important to understand that simply choosing a seat within this range doesn't automatically make your bathroom ADA-compliant. The actual requirements can vary quite a bit depending on your local building codes and whether your shower seat installation is part of a larger project aiming for full accessibility compliance. For example, some codes might have specific requirements for grab bar placement in conjunction with the seat. It’s not just about the height, but also about the seat's design, how far it projects into the shower, and its weight capacity. If you're looking to meet specific accessibility standards or just want to make sure your shower seat is installed perfectly for your needs, bringing in a seasoned pro like HH Remodeling LLC is a smart move. We can ensure everything is up to snuff and safe for everyone using your shower.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
}